   "place": "A working town of about 8,000 people in the valleys of the Algar and Guadalest rivers, 10 km inland from Altea, ringed by the Aitana, Bèrnia and Xortà ranges. It's Spain's main loquat-growing town, with terraced orchards climbing the hillsides. The Fonts de l'Algar, a string of waterfalls and pools on the river Algar, is the best-known sight, and the hills around are popular walking country.",
   "living": "A real town that lives all year rather than a resort, with the beaches of Altea and the bigger towns of the Costa Blanca about a quarter of an hour away.",
   "wiki": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Callosa_d%27en_Sarri%C3%A0",
