   "place": "A small town of about 8,000 people on the river Genil, just upstream of Granada and on the city's bus network. It sits at about 750 m on the road up into the Sierra Nevada, so the high mountains are close above it and the Alhambra, old town and tapas bars of Granada are a short trip below.",
   "living": "A practical, lived-in place rather than a pretty village: mostly modern housing for people who work in Granada. Winters are cold for Andalucía, with a January average of about 6 °C, though the afternoons are often sunny.",
   "wiki": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cenes_de_la_Vega",
