   "place": "The old hill town of Arona, at about 600 m, is the centre of a municipality that runs down to the big resorts of Los Cristianos and Playa de las Américas on Tenerife's sunny south coast. Up here it's quieter: a church square shaded by trees, old farming terraces and volcanic hills. Beaches, restaurants and the ferry to La Gomera are at Los Cristianos below.",
   "living": "The coast is mostly holiday flats and very busy; the hill villages are more Canarian and residential. It's mild all year, with no winter shutdown, but the south of Tenerife is dry and its hills brown for much of the year.",
   "wiki": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arona%2C_Tenerife",
   "qid": "Q698246",
