   "place": "A white village of about 5,700 people in Gran Canaria's north-west, at the mouth of a green valley that runs up towards the pine forest of Tamadaba. Its little port, Puerto de las Nieves, has fish restaurants and the ferry to Tenerife, and the valley grows tropical fruit and coffee.",
   "living": "Quiet and traditional compared with the big resorts of the south. It's mild all year, though the north-west is cloudier than the south and the sea a little cooler.",
