   "place": "A white hill village of about 3,800 people at 640 m in the Axarquía, 18 km above the Costa del Sol, under the Sierra de Almijara and La Maroma (2,065 m), the highest peak of the Sierra de Tejeda. It's known for its wine, celebrated every 15 August at the Noche del Vino, and for walking in the Sierras de Tejeda, Almijara y Alhama Natural Park.",
   "living": "Many residents come from the UK and elsewhere in northern Europe, so there's an established foreign community. The coast at Torrox and Nerja is a short drive down the mountain road.",
   "wiki": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C%C3%B3mpeta",
