   "place": "A town of about 12,900 people in the Maresme, just inland from Mataró and about 30 km north-east of Barcelona, at the foot of the coastal hills. It was a summer retreat for Barcelona families and keeps their modernista houses, including Puig i Cadafalch's own, and a museum of water jugs with four pieces by Picasso. The beaches of the Maresme coast are a few kilometres away.",
   "living": "A commuter town as much as a holiday one, lived in all year, with trains to Barcelona from Mataró next door.",
   "wiki": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argentona",
