   "place": "A village of about 3,200 people on the river Llobregat at the foot of Montserrat, the jagged massif whose Benedictine monastery is one of Catalonia's best-known sights. A rack railway climbs from the village to the monastery, the mountain has some of the region's best walking, and the bridge over the river dates from the 14th century.",
   "living": "Day visitors fill the mountain, but the village itself is quiet and lived in all year. Trains run to Barcelona every half hour.",
   "wiki": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monistrol_de_Montserrat",
