   "place": "A small mountain parish of about 450 people in the Serra de Arga, inland from Viana do Castelo in Portugal's green north-west, the Minho. Stone villages and watermills in the valleys, and granite moorland with horses grazing and wind turbines on the tops. Viana do Castelo, an old port with Atlantic beaches, is the nearest town.",
   "living": "Very rural, with few shops or services in the parish itself. The Minho is the wettest part of Portugal: it's green because it rains a lot from autumn to spring.",
