   "place": "A tiny seaside parish of about 500 people on Madeira's south-west coast, squeezed between the Atlantic and steep cliffs and planted almost entirely with bananas. It has a pebble beach and seafront road, and paragliders land here from the cliffs above. Ponta do Sol and Calheta, with its marina and sandy beach, are a few minutes along the coast.",
   "living": "A parish this small has few homes for sale, so it's worth looking along the coast too. The south-west coast is one of the sunniest parts of Madeira.",
