   "place": "The old Moorish capital of the Algarve, a town of about 6,300 people on the river Arade, crowned by a red sandstone castle and a Gothic cathedral. Orange groves and low hills surround it, the Via Algarviana long-distance path crosses the hills to the north, and the beaches at Armação de Pêra and Portimão are on the coast to the south.",
   "living": "A real town that lives all year, and a member of the Cittaslow network of slow towns, with the busy coast close but not on the doorstep.",
